Z||000000||Mickey_Moose||08-24-2001||11:30 AM||||88 V6 with an automatic transmission.<P>Cold &gt;&gt; when started first time in the morning, starts quick and idles ok, but when I go to drive and step on the brake (say from backing out of the driveway) the car will almost stall and then backfires - ok once warmed up.<P>Warm &gt;&gt; does not start right away once the engine is warm. If I shut the car off and start it right away it's ok, but say it sits for 5 minutes or more, it has to crank a bit to start - sometimes I have to hold the gas pedal down. Noticed a gas smell once it starts.<P>Recently replaced: plugs, wires, cap, rotor, module, EGR tube<P>suggestions?!?!?!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>thanks<BR>Tim||||reg||9
